Get the current list of blocks (records) that make up a page, in the order they appear on it. Each block comes with its recordid and its tplid (block template) — use the recordid with edit_record, update_record or delete_record, and as afterid/beforeid in add_record to insert a new block in the right place. This is the map of the page: it tells you which blocks are there and in what order, not what they say. To read the texts and images of a block use edit_record, and to see how a single block is rendered use get_record_html.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__tilda__get_page_records(args: {
  // Optional. When true, each block additionally carries its rendered html together with the css, js and libraries it pulls in. That makes the response very large — a single block can be thousands of tokens — so turn it on only when you really need the rendered markup of the whole page at once; for one block prefer get_record_html. Defaults to false.
  include_html?: boolean;
  // ID of the page, from get_pages.
  pageid: number;
  // ID of the project that contains the page, from get_projects.
  projectid: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

