Add a block (record) to a page from a block template. tplid is the block template ID from tpls_list: a number like 205, or a variation id like 1241_0 — variations are separate blocks in the catalogue and are passed exactly as tpls_list returns them. Returns the recordid of the new block. By default, the block is appended to the page. To control its position, use beforeid or afterid with the recordid of an adjacent block from get_page_records: afterid inserts the new block AFTER the specified block, while beforeid inserts it BEFORE the specified block.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__tilda__add_record(args: {
  // Optional ID of the block after which to insert the new block.
  afterid?: number;
  // Optional ID of the block before which to insert the new block.
  beforeid?: number;
  // ID of the page to which the block will be added.
  pageid: number;
  // ID of the project that contains the page, from get_projects.
  projectid: number;
  // Block template ID from tpls_list: 205 or a variation id like "1241_0".
  tplid: number | string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

