Get the rendered html of a single block (record) of a page — the markup as it is produced from the block's current content and settings, including unpublished changes. Use it to check the result of an edit on one block without pulling the whole page: it is far cheaper than page_preview or get_page_records with include_html. Returns JSON: "html" — the markup of the block; "css" and "js" — the code of the block template; "jslibs" and "csslibs" — names of the libraries the block needs, files at https://static.tildacdn.com/js/<name> and https://static.tildacdn.com/css/<name>; "tplid". Together with the page scripts https://static.tildacdn.com/js/tilda-scripts-3.0.min.js they are enough to open the block alone in a browser and check its layout without publishing the page.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__tilda__get_record_html(args: {
  // ID of the page that contains the block.
  pageid: number;
  // ID of the project that contains the page, from get_projects.
  projectid: number;
  // ID of the block, from get_page_records or add_record.
  recordid: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

