Save (update) a block's data — this tool saves BOTH the CONTENT fields (texts, images… Call describe_tool with tool_name="update_record" for the full description before using.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__tilda__update_record(args: {
  // Map of "field_name => value", using the field names edit_record returned for the tab. With "only_field" it carries just that one field. Without "only_field" it carries the fields to write for a single tab (content OR settings); fields you do not include keep their current values, so send "" explicitly to clear a field.
  fields: { [key: string]: unknown; };
  // Name of the single field to save. When set, only this field is written and the rest of the block keeps its current values. Prefer it for small, targeted edits; omit it to write several fields of the tab at once.
  only_field?: string;
  // ID of the page that contains the block.
  pageid: number;
  // ID of the project that contains the page, from get_projects.
  projectid: number;
  // The block anchor — a system property available for EVERY block regardless of its tplid. Pass a short latin slug without the "#" (for example "about" or "pricing") to name the block, so links can point at it as "#about" on the same page or "/page-url#about" from another page. Pass an empty string to remove the anchor. Omit it to keep the current anchor: it is never cleared implicitly, not even in whole-tab mode. To change nothing but the anchor, set "only_field" to "rec_anchor" and send an empty "fields".
  rec_anchor?: string;
  // ID of the block to update.
  recordid: number;
  // Editor tab to read. "content": texts, images, links, icons, and similar content fields. "settings": typography, font styles/colors, buttons, cards, spacing, background color, and similar design/layout options. Defaults to "content".
  tab: "content" | "settings";
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

